{"chunk_id": "a2e3b081d626", "text": "After the mourning rites for the dead king, Bhishma, Kunti, and the court perform the sraddha ceremony and distribute gifts to Brahmanas before returning to Hastinapura. Yet grief still fills the kingdom. The sage Vyasa warns his mother Satyavati that the age is declining and that the Kuru dynasty will end through injustice; urging her to avoid witnessing its destruction, he advises her to retire to the forest. She departs with her daughters\u2011in\u2011law and eventually dies in ascetic contemplation. Meanwhile the young Pandavas grow up among the Kauravas, and Bhima\u2019s immense strength dominates their childhood games\u2014he drags, throws, and humiliates Dhritarashtra\u2019s sons. These displays ignite Duryodhana\u2019s jealousy and fear, leading him to secretly plan Bhima\u2019s murder. He arranges a luxurious riverside pleasure house on the Ganga as the setting for his treacherous plot.\nAfter Pandu\u2019s funeral rites, Vyasa warns of the dynasty\u2019s doom, Bhima bullies the Kauravas in childhood, and Duryodhana plots to kill him.\nThemes: mourning and rites, prophecy of decline, childhood rivalry, jealousy and ambition, deception and plotting", "vector": [0.0017336069140583277, -0.01774616912007332, -0.006961541716009378, 0.0051754009909927845, -0.014126438647508621, 0.038908712565898895, -0.01598375290632248, -0.008859527297317982, -0.005514326971024275, -0.025555025786161423, 0.013563821092247963, 0.0008655324345454574, 0.021677711978554726, 0.014370465651154518, -0.006029495038092136, 0.01144892256706953, 0.038854483515024185, 0.0046534547582268715, 0.03964079171419144, -0.024429790675640106, -0.007585165556520224, -0.00021648903202731162, 0.008995098061859608, 0.015549927949905396, -0.020308449864387512, 0.016051538288593292, 0.015441471710801125, -0.024877173826098442, 0.008276574313640594, -0.01450603548437357, -0.009584829211235046, -0.01853247731924057, 0.006344696041196585, -0.015658384189009666, -0.0215150